1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To America 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/115550683/ragnhild-thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Roland Record, Thursday December 7, 1922
2 CONT
2 CONT EARLY PIONEER PASSES AWAY
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Aslak Thompson Passed Away Last Monday at the Age of Ninety-One Years. One of the Early Pioneers of This Place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Aslak Thompson, nee Ragnhild Jacobsdatter Aabo, was born in Sevde, in Ryfylke, Norway, on January 13, 1831, and died at her home in Roland on December 4, 1922, thereby being 91 years, 10 months and 21 days old. She emigrated 
2 CONC from Norway in 1858 and settled in Lisbon, Ill. On November 14, 1858, she was united in marriage to Aslak Thompson the ceremony performed by Rev. P. A. Rasmussen. In the spring of 1865, they moved west and settled on the Thompson 
2 CONC farm south of Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT They marriage was blessed with 9 children of which 4 are dead. Besides the husband, 5 children mourn the departed: Mrs. John Nereim, Abel Thompson and Oscar Thompson of this place; Mrs. John Halvorson of Dallas, Wis., and Mrs. Hen
2 CONC ry Stole of Forest City; also 36 grandchildren and 19 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services are being conducted from Bergen Lutheran church this afternoon. She has been a faithful member of this congregation and attended meetings regularly until later years when she has been unable to do so because of fr
2 CONC ail health.
2 CONT
2 CONT Card of Thanks
2 CONT
2 CONT To the kind neighbors and friends who so willingly assisted and comforted us during the sickness and death of our beloved wife and mother, we wish to express our heartfelt thanks, also to those sending flowers and assisting in the
2 CONC  music. May the Lord's blessing be with you all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. John Nereim
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. John Halvorson
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Henry Stole
2 CONT Able Thompson
2 CONT Oscar Thompson
2 CONT A. B. Anderson
2 CONT Mrs. Lena Thompson
2 CONT and families
2 CONT ——-
