1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/genealogy/Lilleg%C3%A5rd-Family-Tree-1
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.myheritage.com/names/olea_iversdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT https://forum.arkivverket.no/topic/185202-kittel-nilsen-fca-1814-i-aal-buskerud/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT After his wife died, Kittil was left with three children.  He later married Olea Iversdotter Lislerud of Renli in Valdres.  In 1867 Kittil's three children by his first marriage came to America.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1870's all of the other children except Iver and Ingebjor came to Minnesota.  In 1887 Iver also came, so only Ingebjor remained in Norway.  Asle lived for a while in Canada and "young Kittil" in North Dakota, but both retur
2 CONC ned to Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1868 he sold North Veslegard at auction and he and his wife moved to Strauman, a farm that is now covered by Tunnhodfjorden, where they lived as tenants.  They became very poor and had to ask for public assistance.  In 1870 Ole
2 CONC a died and in 1873 he came to America to be with his children.  He died in Northern Minnesota in 1902
